/* ---- container ---- */
.card-grid {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 1.5rem;                        /* 24px between cards */
  padding: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* ---- card ---- */
.card {
  /* grow from basis, never shrink below basis, base = a third minus the two gaps */
  flex: 1 1 calc((100% - 2 * 1.5rem) / 3);
  min-width: 0;                       /* lets long words/children shrink instead of overflowing */
  box-sizing: border-box;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;             /* so footers can be pushed down with margin-top:auto */
  padding: 1.25rem;
  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
  border-radius: 12px;
  background: #fff;
  overflow-wrap: break-word;
}

.card > :last-child { margin-top: auto; }   /* optional: align card footers */

/* ---- 3 → 1 collapse ---- */
@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
  .card-grid { gap: 1rem; }
  .card { flex-basis: 100%; }         /* or flex: 1 1 100% */
}

/* ---- optional two-column middle step ---- */
@media (min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023.98px) {
  .card { flex-basis: calc((100% - 1.5rem) / 2); }
}
```

```html
<div class="card-grid">
  <article class="card"><h2>Title</h2><p>Body text.</p><a href="#">Action</a></article>
  <article class="card"><h2>Title</h2><p>Body text.</p><a href="#">Action</a></article>
  <article class="card"><h2>Title</h2><p>Body text.</p><a href="#">Action</a></article>
</div>
```

The details that make it work:

- **`flex-basis` must subtract the gaps.** With `gap` the browser doesn't reduce the basis for you, so three `33.333%` cards plus two 24px gaps overflow and wrap into 2-1. `calc((100% - 2 * gap) / 3)` is exact.
- **`flex: 1 1 basis` lets a short last row stretch.** If you have 4 cards, the final one grows to fill the row. If you'd rather it keep the column width, use `flex: 0 1 <basis>` — then the last row is left-aligned with empty space.
- **`min-width: 0`** is the fix for the classic Flexbox overflow: flex items default to `min-width: auto`, so an unbreakable string or a wide `<pre>`/`<img>` blows the card past its basis.
- **`767.98px`, not `768px`**, avoids the one-pixel overlap where both the mobile and tablet rules match on fractional device pixel ratios.
- With `box-sizing: border-box` on the cards, padding and borders stay inside the computed basis, so the three-across arithmetic holds.

If you can target modern browsers only, `display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr))` does the same job in two lines — but it produces as many columns as fit, not a fixed 3→1, so the Flexbox version above is the right tool when the breakpoint is specified.

